# GitHub token for /api/github.
#
# Optional locally (unauthenticated works at 60 req/hr per IP), but REQUIRED in
# production: on Vercel the outbound IP is shared with other tenants, so the
# unauthenticated limit gets exhausted by traffic that isn't yours.
#
# Create at github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens → Fine-grained token:
#   Repository access: Public Repositories (read-only)
#   Account permissions: none
# It can only read data that is already public, so a leak is near-harmless.
#
# Set the same value in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables
# (Production + Preview + Development).
#
# Do NOT prefix with VITE_ — that would inline it into the client bundle.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
